    "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45373": {
      "title": "ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT/CMU ONLINE",
      "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT/CMU ONLINE Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary’s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT/CMU ONLINE Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU’s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3942 Position Number 78840 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT/CMU ONLINE Position Summary The Associate Vice President ( AVP ) has oversight of the academic unit within the CMU Online Learning enterprise. In partnership with academic colleges, departments, and university stakeholders, the AVP supports the development, delivery, and growth of online, hybrid, and off-campus academic and professional learning opportunities. The AVP collaborates with faculty and academic leadership to advance credit and noncredit programming, including undergraduate, graduate, certificate, micro-credential, and professional development offerings. The position also oversees prior learning initiatives, competency-based education efforts, and select interdisciplinary programs administered through CMU Online. The AVP is responsible for growing the number of academic and noncredit programs delivered online and at distance, working with outreach teams to grow customized learning solutions, dual enrollment, and community college partnerships, and expanding and developing alternative routes to credit through prior learning, competency based, and other progressive approaches. Reporting to the vice president of CMU Online, the AVP advances innovative, accessible, and student-centered learning opportunities aligned with the university’s strategic priorities. Required Qualifications Terminal degree from a regionally accredited institution. Five years of progressively advanced leadership experience in higher education or a related field. Demonstrated experience building and sustaining partnerships with academic leaders, faculty, administrators, and external stakeholders. Demonstrated success leading strategic initiatives, organizational change, and cross-functional collaboration within complex organizations. Demonstrated commitment to ensuring that all members of the university community can thrive. Demonstrated understanding of best practices in pedagogical and instruction in online and post-traditional higher education. Knowledge of emerging trends, technologies, and practices related to online learning, and workforce-aligned programming in higher education. Demonstrated ability to analyze data, assess operational effectiveness, and support strategic decision-making. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and executive presentation skills, with the ability to effectively represent the university at state, regional, and national levels. Preferred Qualifications Terminal degree in postsecondary education, educational leadership, learning design, curriculum and instruction, training and development, or a related field from an accredited institution. Demonstrated experience supporting academic program development, online and alternative learning initiatives, curriculum innovation, and student-centered educational programming for post-traditional learners. Postsecondary teaching and faculty experience. Familiarity with a collective bargaining environment. Demonstrated experience developing noncredit programs, prior learning, micro-credentials, stackable credentials, certificates, and lifelong learning initiatives. Expertise in compliance, budgeting, enrollment management, curriculum, online learning environments, and LMS technologies. Demonstrated experience leading and managing externally sponsored projects. Duties & Responsibilities Provides executive leadership for the strategic growth, development, and oversight of credit, noncredit, and alternative academic programming across face-to-face, hybrid, and online modalities within CMU Online. Oversees the administration and expansion of undergraduate, graduate, certificate, professional development, micro-credential, digital badge, and alternative pathway programs, including stackable and certification-to-credit initiatives. Supports the vice president of CMU Online in representing the university at state, national, and international levels on matters related to online learning, innovation, and distance education. Provides leadership in the interpretation, implementation, and continuous improvement of academic programming policies, procedures, and operational practices related to online and continuing education. Serves as a collaborative leader within the university’s curricular and shared governance processes through active participation on institutional committees and councils. Develops and support strategies to increase enrollment, retention, persistence, and graduation outcomes. Collaborates with academic and administrative units to improve the student experience. Analyzes enrollment trends, market demands, and student success data to inform decision-making. Advances initiatives focused on adult learners, online education, transfer students, and workforce-aligned programming. Provides strategic oversight of the Prior Learning Assessment, Fire Up Forward dual enrollment activities, and Central Bound dual-admission/co-enrollment transfer program. Leads the development and coordination of curricular materials and program proposals for internal review and external stakeholder engagement. Fosters strong partnerships with academic colleges, departments, and program directors to advance innovative delivery models and alternative credentialing opportunities. Utilizes data analytics and assessment practices to evaluate effectiveness and guide strategic decisions. Prepares reports, presentations, and recommendations for senior leadership, governing boards, and external stakeholders. Monitors key performance indicators related to enrollment, operations, finances, and student outcomes. Supports the vice president in representing CMU Online in university related events, ceremonial engagements, and activities. Collaborates across the university to strengthen academic programming, student success initiatives, faculty support, and operational effectiveness within online and distance education. Cultivates and expands partnerships with external stakeholders to support workforce alignment and program growth. Develops and/or strengthens external partnerships with alumni, businesses, government, and service organizations, along with other internal and external constituents. Collaborates in the development of new and innovative support services for off-campus students in online learning. Responsible for setting the academic calendar for professional development for faculty, staff, and students related to innovation, student engagement, and online learning in collaboration with CMU Online’s management team. Establishes and assesses operational goals, performance measures, and service standards. Promotes process improvement, operational efficiency, and data-informed decision-making. Ensures compliance with university policies, accreditation standards, and state/federal regulations. Provides administrative leadership and operational oversight for the academic unit within CMU Online, including program effectiveness, assessment, and performance outcomes. Supports CMU Online’s strategic marketing, outreach, operational planning, and continuous process improvement initiatives. Fosters a culture of innovation, collaboration, and student-centered excellence across the university community. Performs additional duties and strategic initiatives as assigned by the vice president. Supervision Exercised Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. The Leadership Standards define how we lead and treat others on our team. As leaders, it is our responsibility to seek input from our teams to continuously improve our leadership abilities and our demonstration of the standards. Additionally, it is our responsibility to encourage and support the growth and development of those whom we lead. At CMU , we encourage employees to grow both personally and professionally, and thus advance CMU’s culture of excellence. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU’s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Senior Officer Staff Pay Level Pay Range $150,000 - $160,000 Division Academic Affairs Department CMU ONLINE Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Typically Mon-Fri 8-5; evenings and weekends as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master’s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men’s and women’s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It’s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state’s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions — Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more — are within easy reach of the city’s central location in Michigan’s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see “Know Your Rights ” posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU’s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education’s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU’s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity?  Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong?  (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position and click “Yes” if you understand and support the culture that is important to CMU. Yes No * Do you have a terminal degree from a regionally accredited institution? Yes No * Do you have at least five years of progressively advanced leadership experience in higher education or a related field? Yes No * Do you have experience building and sustaining partnerships with academic leaders, faculty, administrators, and external stakeholders? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution.  CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright © Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
